Conclusion and evidence boundary:
- The reference state-machine result is now backed by a real PostgreSQL/FORCE-RLS and real HTTP/TCP integration path with two server processes.
- Idempotency, change-log insertion and attachment persistence remained consistent under concurrent requests.
- The 100ms/10Mbps link is deterministic application-level emulation over loopback, not a carrier/Wi-Fi field trace. Production deployment must rerun the same scenario through its ingress, TLS, pooler, object store and chosen regional network before release acceptance.
- Payload shape is a load-spike contract, not the production BFF HTTP runtime; the production runtime/pool driver remains a separate M6 integration item.
